/**
 * The public demo film (brief §18).
 *
 * "FRAME Demo Film" exists so someone can see what FRAME actually is before
 * signing up for anything. It is a complete worked example — story, vision,
 * Visual DNA, world bible, scenes, shots and composed prompts — so the
 * pipeline the landing page describes can be walked end to end.
 *
 * Two properties matter:
 *
 *   · No API key is needed to explore it. Every prompt below is produced by
 *     the deterministic prompt engine from this material; nothing here was
 *     generated by a model and nothing here calls one.
 *
 *   · It is read-only for everyone. `is_demo = 1`, and `access.mjs` refuses
 *     every write against it, so no visitor can spoil it for the next.
 *
 * Seeding is idempotent: the film is created once and then left alone, so a
 * redeploy never duplicates it or overwrites edits made to the seed by hand.
 */
